\ orbit.fg — two-body orbit integrated with symplectic (semi-implicit) Euler.
\ Units: G*M = 1.  Prints position every 1000 steps and the relative energy drift,
\ which stays bounded for a symplectic integrator (it would grow with explicit Euler).
\ Run:  ./forge core.fg examples/orbit.fg

variable x   variable y   variable vx   variable vy
1.0 x !   0.0 y !   0.0 vx !   1.1 vy !          \ slightly eccentric orbit
0.001 constant dt

: r2      ( -- r^2 )   x @ fsquare y @ fsquare f+ ;
: energy  ( -- E )     vx @ fsquare vy @ fsquare f+ 0.5 f*  1.0 r2 fsqrt f/ f- ;
: accel   ( -- ax ay ) r2 dup fsqrt f* 1.0 swap f/ fnegate  dup x @ f* swap y @ f* ;
: step    ( -- )
    accel  dt f* vy @ f+ vy !   dt f* vx @ f+ vx !     \ kick: v += a dt
    vx @ dt f* x @ f+ x !   vy @ dt f* y @ f+ y ! ;     \ drift: x += v dt

energy constant E0
: report ( step -- )
    6 .r ."   x=" x @ f. ."  y=" y @ f. ."  v=" vx @ fsquare vy @ fsquare f+ fsqrt f.
    ."  dE/E=" energy E0 f- E0 f/ fabs f. cr ;

." symplectic Euler two-body orbit, dt=" dt f. cr
0 report
: run  10 1 do  1000 0 do step loop  i 1000 * report  loop ;
run
bye
